AB  - To be resilient and lasting, modern system archi-tectures need to fulfill multiple non-functional requirements simultaneously, including security, availability, and maintainability. Traditional static security design approaches are no longer sufficient in the midst of continually evolving cybersecurity threats and rapidly changing regulatory landscapes. This paper presents Security Architecture as a Service (SAaaS), a framework that uses visual modeling and trade-off analysis to integrate security, compliance, and resilience into system lifecycles. The framework is particularly relevant for regulated industries such as financial services, where continuous compliance and resilience are critical.
ER  - 

