AB  - Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) systems face significant challenges in reliably detecting anomalies and in swift identification of root causes, especially when handling massive log volumes from enterprise and IoT environments. While traditional heuristic methods and rule-based approaches struggle with accuracy, recent developments leveraging Large Language Models (LLM) offer promising improvements. However, practical adoption remains limited due to computational complexity, interpretability issues, privacy concerns and stringent security requirements. To bridge this gap, we introduce JAVELIN, a novel Java based microservices architecture designed for real time, privacy aware and semantically rich $\log$ analytics. JAVELIN integrates the LangChain4j framework with dynamic metadata enrichment, adaptive active learning, and differential privacy techniques. By utilizing flexible cloud GPU offloading, JAVELIN supports advanced analytical capabilities even on resource-constrained environments. Our rigorous evaluation on standard benchmarks (LogHub and CIC-IoT-2023) demonstrates significant improvements over baseline heuristic methods, achieving an anomaly detection accuracy of 98.1%. Additionally, JAVELIN consistently exhibits superior clustering quality and generates semantically coherent and contextually relevant log explanations. These results underscore JAVELIN’s effectiveness, scalability, and adaptability as a comprehensive, secure, and interpretable analytical solution for real-time log anomaly detection and root-cause analysis.
ER  - 

